 "mode": "physiology",
 "description": "A model of blood vessels. A pressure source of 100 mmHg drives blood through an artery (in series) and then through two vascular beds side by side (in parallel). The flowmeters show how the flow divides: more flow takes the path of lower resistance. Total resistance = <i>R</i><sub>artery</sub> + 1 / (1/<i>R</i><sub>A</sub> + 1/<i>R</i><sub>B</sub>), and flow = difference in pressure / resistance (Darcy’s law, the same form as Ohm’s law). Try narrowing bed A (raise its resistance) and see where the flow goes.",
